[quote="Foote"]

<b>Braithwhite wrote:</b>
<div class="bb-quote"><blockquote class="bb-quote-body">Step A- deal all targets 1 energy damage. &nbsp;apply any buffs/resistances as needed.Step B- You MAY deal any target that took damage from step A, 1 (one) energy damage, applying buffs/resistances as needed. &nbsp;You can do this on a case by case basis.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</blockquote></div>
Well, you have to do it on a case by case basis. You do not deal all targets 1 and THEN decide who gets the extra hits. Hypersonic Assault ruling applies here.&nbsp;

[/quote]

I think that we are arguing the same exact point. &nbsp;Let me re-phrase.

Hypersonic assault requires that everyone who takes damage gets the effect: cannot do damage. &nbsp;

For incidental contact, everyone who takes damage from step A gets the effect: KNYFE may deal this target 1 energy damage.

For each effected (took damage) target (of step A), KNYFE makes the decision (on a case by case basis, predicated on whether or not they took damage in step A) of applying the secondary effect. &nbsp;the secondary effect being that she MAY deal them 1 energy damage (or not, if that is what she decided to do). &nbsp;

Basically, you see who gets hit from the first wave- and then you decide which of that set gets hit again. &nbsp;
